    "## 7. Data Cleaning — Key Decisions\n",
    "\n",
    "### 7.1 Deduplication\n",
    "- The raw CSV has 493 rows.\n",
    "- 7 fully identical rows were removed.\n",
    "- 134 title-level duplicates (same title in different cases, e.g. `DevOps Architect` and `DEVOPS ARCHITECT`) were removed by keeping the first occurrence. These are genuinely the same role described twice with case variation.\n",
    "- **Final dataset: 352 unique IT role definitions.**\n",
    "\n",
    "### 7.2 Category Inference\n",
    "The original dataset has **no category column**. Categories are inferred by matching job titles against a deterministic keyword ruleset (`CATEGORY_RULES` in `src/preprocessing.py`). Rules are checked in priority order — first match wins. Only 7 roles (2%) remain as `Other IT` after the expanded rule set.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 7.3 Skill Parsing\n",
    "Skills are stored as comma-separated strings. Each skill is split, stripped, and normalised via `SKILL_NORMALIZATION` (e.g. `CI/CD` variations, `AWS` synonyms, `Python` variants).\n",
    "\n",
    "### 7.4 Certification Parsing\n",
    "Certifications are parsed the same way. Special characters from PDF encoding (e.g. `â€"` for em-dashes) are preserved as-is since they do not affect analysis."
   ]
  },
