    "## 12. Key Insights\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **DevOps & SRE dominates IT roles (24%):** CI/CD, Docker, Kubernetes, AWS, Python, and Automation are the core toolchain for this category.\n",
    "\n",
    "2. **Cloud Computing is the #1 most demanded skill overall** (appears in 82 of 352 roles, 23.3%). This confirms cloud proficiency as a baseline IT competency.\n",
    "\n",
    "3. **Certifications matter for Cloud and Security:** AWS, Azure, and CompTIA certifications are most frequently referenced. Security roles strongly emphasize CISSP, CEH, and CompTIA Security+.\n",
    "\n",
    "4. **AI/ML requires Python + Cloud:** The AI/ML skill profile is dominated by Cloud Computing, Machine Learning, Python, and Deep Learning — reinforcing that cloud infrastructure is inseparable from modern AI work.\n",
    "\n",
    "5. **Skill Co-occurrence:** CI/CD + Automation, Cloud Computing + AWS, and Kubernetes + Docker are the strongest co-occurring pairs — IT skills cluster around specific toolchains.\n",
    "\n",
    "6. **ML Classification (72.9% accuracy with Linear SVM):** The model correctly distinguishes IT categories from description text, with Security (F1=0.86) and DevOps & SRE (F1=0.70) performing best.\n",
    "\n",
    "7. **Category Skill Signatures are clear:** Scripting is DevOps-specific, Financial Analysis appears only in Management, SQL and ETL are Data-specific."
   ]
